<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
  <!-- Generated theme ramp. Every colour literal the app used to hard-code,
       keyed by its own System-theme hex so AppThemeService can recolour it
       without the source value ever being lost. Keeping each shade separate
       (rather than collapsing them onto the named tokens in Tokens.axaml) is
       what preserves the depth the UI was drawn with.

       Three roles, decided by chroma rather than HSL saturation - saturation
       explodes near white and would file near-white text as a colour:

         Surface_*   neutral blue-grey, lightness <= 0.55. Hue-shifted by the
                     dark presets; inverted by the light ones.
         Text_*      neutral blue-grey, lightness > 0.55, plus the muted text
                     values below the split. Untouched by the dark presets -
                     text colours stay put for readability - and inverted by
                     the light ones, which would otherwise be white on white.
         Semantic_*  everything with real colour: the greens, reds and ambers
                     that mean something. Never re-hued, only inverted for
                     light mode so they stay legible on a pale surface.

       Pure greys and white/black overlays carry no hue to shift and are left
       as literals at their call sites. -->

  <!-- Surfaces, borders and fills -->
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Surface_05080B" Color="#05080B" />
  <SolidColorBrush x:Key="Surface_0B0F14" Color="#0B0F14" />
